course: dictionary
lesson: 5980
title: Short as a mayfly
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mayfly is a delicate insect. Delicate means light, thin and easily damaged, so think of its see-through wings and long tails.
explain: A mayfly has two parts to its life. «Mayflies live a year or more as nymphs under water,» and then the adult flies out into the air. A nymph is a young mayfly.
explain: The adult stage is very short. «An adult mayfly may live only a day» is the key clue: the sentence compares it with trees that are «nearly 5,000 years old», so you can tell a day is very short.
fact: A mayfly is an insect with see-through wings and long tails.
fact: A mayfly nymph lives under water for a year or more.
fact: An adult mayfly often lives only a day or less.
fact: «As short-lived as a mayfly» means lasting a very short time.
fact: Mayfly nymphs in a stream show that the water is clean.
exercise: A mayfly is a delicate insect with see-through wings. What does delicate mean? | Loud and noisy | Very hungry | Brightly coloured with thick fur | *Light and easily damaged
exercise: «An adult mayfly may live only a day.» Find the word that shows its life is short. | pine | *only | some | nearly
exercise: «Mayflies live a year or more as nymphs under water.» Where do mayfly nymphs live? | In the air | *Under water | Inside a tree | On the top of a hill
test: Mayfly nymphs are found in a stream. What do they show? | *The water is clean | There are no fish | The stream is empty | The water is hot
test: «Her plan was as short-lived as a mayfly.» What does this mean? | It grew very tall | It travelled very far | It lasted for hundreds of years | *It lasted a very short time
exam: A mayfly spends years as a nymph but often only a day or less as an adult. What does this show? | Mayflies never leave the water | Adults live longer than nymphs | Mayflies live as adults for ten years in the air | *Its adult life is very short compared with its life as a nymph
